{
  "summary": "The change fixes the root cause of issue #2283: TypeCollector now skips compiler-generated fields (metadata auto-property backing fields such as <Key>k__BackingField, whose names are not valid C# identifiers) when enumerating members in both key and map mode, and every diagnostic location that indexed DeclaringSyntaxReferences[0] now tolerates symbols without syntax via FirstOrDefault(), with a new GetIdentifierLocation that also handles record primary-constructor ParameterSyntax. On head all new generator and analyzer tests pass (full suite 203/203, no regressions versus base), while on base source 17 of the 31 new tests failed with IndexOutOfRangeException/AD0001 or InvalidCastException, so the fix covers REQ-2283-F1 through F3 and N1/N2. Two observations only: mutation coverage is thin for the new guards, and diagnostics for members of metadata-declared types may carry no location.",
  "requirement_verdicts": [
    {
      "req": "REQ-2283-F1",
      "verdict": "met",
      "confidence_basis": "GeneratorProducesResolver passes for all referenced-library cases on head (including \"struct generic\") and GeneratorCollectsTypeArgumentOfReferencedGenericValueType passes with PayloadFormatter and global::Lib.Item<global::App.Payload> in the generated output; the same new tests failed on base source with IndexOutOfRangeException (the CS8785 path), and the fix filters metadata backing fields out of member enumeration (lines 753/1050) and stops indexing DeclaringSyntaxReferences[0] (line 1077).",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "test", "name": "ReferencedAssemblyTypesTests.GeneratorProducesResolver(caseName: \"struct generic\", libraryDeclaration: \"[MessagePackObject] public partial struct Item<T> \"···)", "outcome": "passed"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "ReferencedAssemblyTypesTests.GeneratorProducesResolver(caseName: \"struct generic\", libraryDeclaration: \"[MessagePackObject] public partial struct Item<T> \"···)", "outcome": "failed", "check": "tests.fail_without_fix"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "ReferencedAssemblyTypesTests.GeneratorCollectsTypeArgumentOfReferencedGenericValueType", "outcome": "passed"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "ReferencedAssemblyTypesTests.GeneratorCollectsTypeArgumentOfReferencedGenericValueType", "outcome": "failed", "check": "tests.fail_without_fix"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 753, "rev": "head", "quote": ".Where(m => m is IFieldSymbol or IPropertySymbol && !(m.IsStatic || m.IsOverride || m.IsImplicitlyDeclared || IsCompilerGeneratedField(m)));"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1050, "rev": "head", "quote": "if (item.IsImplicitlyDeclared || item.IsStatic || IsCompilerGeneratedField(item))"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1077, "rev": "head", "quote": ": Diagnostic.Create(MsgPack00xMessagePackAnalyzer.MemberNeedsKey, item.DeclaringSyntaxReferences.FirstOrDefault()?.GetSyntax(this.cancellationToken).GetLocation(), formattedType.ToDisplayString(SymbolDisplayFormat.FullyQualifiedFormat), item.Name);"},
        {"kind": "check", "id": "tests.fail_without_fix", "status": "pass"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "req": "REQ-2283-F2",
      "verdict": "met",
      "confidence_basis": "AnalyzerDoesNotThrow passes for all library cases on head and failed on base with AD0001/IndexOutOfRangeException; NullStringKey_RecordPrimaryConstructorParameter passes on head and failed on base with InvalidCastException from the (PropertyDeclarationSyntax) cast; BothStringAndIntKeyAreNull now uses GetIdentifierLocation (line 985) and MemberNeedsKey uses FirstOrDefault() (line 1077), both tolerating metadata symbols without syntax.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "test", "name": "ReferencedAssemblyTypesTests.AnalyzerDoesNotThrow(caseName: \"struct generic\", libraryDeclaration: \"[MessagePackObject] public partial struct Item<T> \"···)", "outcome": "passed"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "ReferencedAssemblyTypesTests.AnalyzerDoesNotThrow(caseName: \"struct generic\", libraryDeclaration: \"[MessagePackObject] public partial struct Item<T> \"···)", "outcome": "failed", "check": "tests.fail_without_fix"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "MsgPack00xAnalyzerTests.NullStringKey_RecordPrimaryConstructorParameter", "outcome": "passed"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "MsgPack00xAnalyzerTests.NullStringKey_RecordPrimaryConstructorParameter", "outcome": "failed", "check": "tests.fail_without_fix"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 985, "rev": "head", "quote": "this.reportDiagnostic?.Invoke(Diagnostic.Create(MsgPack00xMessagePackAnalyzer.BothStringAndIntKeyAreNull, GetIdentifierLocation(item), formattedType.ToDisplayString(SymbolDisplayFormat.FullyQualifiedFormat), item.Name));"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 985, "rev": "base", "quote": "((PropertyDeclarationSyntax)item.DeclaringSyntaxReferences[0].GetSyntax()).Identifier.GetLocation(),"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1077, "rev": "base", "quote": "item.DeclaringSyntaxReferences[0].GetSyntax().GetLocation(),"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1077, "rev": "head", "quote": ": Diagnostic.Create(MsgPack00xMessagePackAnalyzer.MemberNeedsKey, item.DeclaringSyntaxReferences.FirstOrDefault()?.GetSyntax(this.cancellationToken).GetLocation(), formattedType.ToDisplayString(SymbolDisplayFormat.FullyQualifiedFormat), item.Name);"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "req": "REQ-2283-F3",
      "verdict": "met",
      "confidence_basis": "AnalyzerStillReportsProblemsInReferencingProject passes on head: exactly one diagnostic, MemberNeedsKey, with Location.IsInSource true; on base it failed because the analyzer threw AD0001 instead of reporting MsgPack004. Diagnostics for metadata-symbol members now resolve to a null location via FirstOrDefault()/GetIdentifierLocation instead of crashing on empty DeclaringSyntaxReferences, so nothing is reported outside the analyzing compilation.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "test", "name": "ReferencedAssemblyTypesTests.AnalyzerStillReportsProblemsInReferencingProject", "outcome": "passed"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "ReferencedAssemblyTypesTests.AnalyzerStillReportsProblemsInReferencingProject", "outcome": "failed", "check": "tests.fail_without_fix"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "ReferencedAssemblyTypesTests.AnalyzerDoesNotThrowOnInvalidReferencedType(libraryDeclaration: \"[MessagePackObject] public partial record struct I\"···)", "outcome": "passed"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1433, "rev": "head", "quote": "private static Location? GetIdentifierLocation(IPropertySymbol property) {"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1077, "rev": "head", "quote": ": Diagnostic.Create(MsgPack00xMessagePackAnalyzer.MemberNeedsKey, item.DeclaringSyntaxReferences.FirstOrDefault()?.GetSyntax(this.cancellationToken).GetLocation(), formattedType.ToDisplayString(SymbolDisplayFormat.FullyQualifiedFormat), item.Name);"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "req": "REQ-2283-N1",
      "verdict": "met",
      "confidence_basis": "Full suite: 203 passed, 0 failed, with no failures not on base and no failures also on base (base 167/167); build passes, no public API changes, no new analyzer warnings.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "check", "id": "tests.full_suite", "status": "pass"},
        {"kind": "check", "id": "build", "status": "pass"},
        {"kind": "check", "id": "public_api", "status": "pass"},
        {"kind": "check", "id": "analyzers", "status": "pass"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "req": "REQ-2283-N2",
      "verdict": "met",
      "confidence_basis": "fail_without_fix reports 17 of 31 new tests failing on base source (new_failed 17 / new_total 31), including every previously crashing GeneratorProducesResolver and AnalyzerDoesNotThrow case, so the fix is covered by tests that fail without it.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "check", "id": "tests.fail_without_fix", "status": "pass"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "ReferencedAssemblyTypesTests.GeneratorProducesResolver(caseName: \"struct generic\", libraryDeclaration: \"[MessagePackObject] public partial struct Item<T> \"···)", "outcome": "failed", "check": "tests.fail_without_fix"}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "F1",
      "title": "Mutation coverage is thin for the new compiler-generated-field guard",
      "severity": "info",
      "category": "tests",
      "claim": "Under the harness rule (only new tests count as kills), mutants at TypeCollector.cs:1050 (M2 negating the guard, M4 dropping it to if (true), M5 swapping || to &&) and at TypeCollector.cs:1455 (M3 making IsCompilerGeneratedField always return false) survived with no killing test; existing tests do fail on M2/M4, but no new test isolates the skipping of metadata auto-property backing fields.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "check", "id": "tests.mutation", "status": "fail"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1050, "rev": "head", "quote": "if (item.IsImplicitlyDeclared || item.IsStatic || IsCompilerGeneratedField(item))"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1455, "rev": "head", "quote": "private static bool IsCompilerGeneratedField(ISymbol member) => member is IFieldSymbol { CanBeReferencedByName: false };"}
      ],
      "suggested_fix": "Add a regression test that observes a metadata auto-property backing field is skipped (for example, require all non-public members in the app and assert no MemberNeedsKey is produced for the imported backing field), or accept the gap: end-to-end tests already fail without the fix and existing tests fail on the guard-negating mutants."
    },
    {
      "id": "F2",
      "title": "Diagnostics for members of metadata-declared types carry no location",
      "severity": "info",
      "category": "correctness",
      "claim": "When a member of a type from a referenced assembly lacks a key, MemberNeedsKey is created with item.DeclaringSyntaxReferences.FirstOrDefault()?.GetSyntax() resolving to null, so the diagnostic has no location in the user's compilation. This does not violate REQ-2283-F3 (no location outside the compilation), but the user cannot navigate to the member, and the behavior is only implicitly covered: AnalyzerDoesNotThrowOnInvalidReferencedType asserts no AD0001, not the absence of null-location diagnostics.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1077, "rev": "head", "quote": ": Diagnostic.Create(MsgPack00xMessagePackAnalyzer.MemberNeedsKey, item.DeclaringSyntaxReferences.FirstOrDefault()?.GetSyntax(this.cancellationToken).GetLocation(), formattedType.ToDisplayString(SymbolDisplayFormat.FullyQualifiedFormat), item.Name);"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "ReferencedAssemblyTypesTests.AnalyzerDoesNotThrowOnInvalidReferencedType(libraryDeclaration: \"[MessagePackObject] public partial record struct I\"···)", "outcome": "passed"}
      ],
      "suggested_fix": "Decide whether to suppress MemberNeedsKey for metadata-declared members with no syntax, or document that such diagnostics have no location."
    }
  ],
  "refusals": [
    {
      "topic": "Security impact on runtime deserialization of untrusted input",
      "reason": "The diff touches only compile-time generator/analyzer diagnostics (TypeCollector.cs) and tests; no runtime serialization or deserialization code is modified, so no runtime security behaviour can be judged from this evidence.",
      "who_should_decide": "area owner (security review only if a future change touches runtime deserialization)",
      "blocking": false
    }
  ],
  "refutations": []
}
